From 1a294a2aaa37a791e0f5a20e4409a8673aa6681a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:33:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0220 -- count the mouse presses the level poll
 never saw

WHY: DOSVESA_PumpEvents reads the buttons as a level (INT 33h function 3)
once per pump. A press and release that both land between two pumps never
become a button-down event: the click is gone, with no trace in any log.
At 40 pumps/s the gap is 25 ms and a human click survives it; at the 6 fps
the 640x480 intro runs at on the 486 the gap is ~170 ms and quick clicks
vanish (real hardware, 2026-09-15/16: the operator had to hold the button
down across a poll). A journey metric for click response cannot see this
from the engine side -- a click that never arrives has no start event -- so
a lost click has to be counted where it is lost, or a "click latency" p95
would improve exactly when clicks start disappearing. The same poll hides
the wait of a click that does survive: its event is stamped when the pump
sees it, not when the button went down, so a journey that starts at the
event timestamp is short by up to one pump gap -- ~170 ms at 6 fps, the
very case the metric exists for.

WHAT: the mouse driver keeps its own per-button press count (function 5,
"button press information": presses since the last call). The pump now
counts the up->down edges of the left and right buttons its own level read
sees (seen), and every 8th pump reads the driver's counts (hw; two more
real-mode INT 33h calls, so ~5 reads/s at 40 fps). SDL_DOSMouseClickStats()
(new header SDL_dosinput_stats.h) takes one more driver read and returns
hw, seen and the read count; the port reports lost = hw - seen. The totals
are cumulative, so the read cadence does not change them. It can read -1
transiently (a button held when the driver was reset; a press between the
last pump and the final read). The pump also records its own start time
(one SDL_GetTicksNS per pump) in a 16-entry ring, and
SDL_DOSInputWaitBoundNS(event_ts) returns the event's timestamp minus the
start of the pump before the one that stamped it: an upper bound on the
unseen wait, 0 when the pump has left the ring. Counting only: no event is
synthesised and input delivery is unchanged. Main thread only; nothing
runs in an ISR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosinput_stats.h | 98 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosevents.c     | 94 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 192 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/SDL3/SDL_dosinput_stats.h

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosinput_stats.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosinput_stats.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2394a6623
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosinput_stats.h
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+/*
+  Simple DirectMedia Layer
